_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":11.1,"_gate_share_shrink":0.194118659664972,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":null,"_gp_sbc_dilution":null,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.109919995,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":73.3,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Allogene Therapeutics, Inc. a clinical stage immuno-oncology company, develops and commercializes genetically engineered allogeneic T cell therapies for the treatment of cancer and autoimmune diseases. It develops a pipeline of multiple allogeneic CAR T cell product candidates utilizing protein engineering, gene editing, gene insertion, and advanced proprietary T cell manufacturing technologies. The company is also developing cemacabtagene ansegedleucel (cema-cel), an engineered allogeneic CAR T cell product candidate that targets CD19 for the treatment of large B-cell lymphoma (LBCL). In addition, it develops ALLO-316, an engineered allogeneic CAR T cell product candidate that targets CD70 to treat renal cell carcinoma (RCC); and ALLO-329, an engineered allogeneic CAR T cell product candidate that targets both CD19 and CD70 for the treatment of autoimmune diseases (AID), such as systemic lupus erythematosus (SLE), idiopathic inflammatory myopathies (IIM), and systemic sclerosis (SSc). The company was incorporated in 2017 and is headquartered in South San Francisco, California.","ceo_bio":"Dr. Zachary J. Roberts M.D., Ph.D. | President, CEO & Director | Age 47 | Compensation: $750,761 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 150 people. Stock-based compensation of $251K per employee reflects an ownership culture. Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (9/10).","financial_summary":["Allogene Therapeutics, Inc. is a micro-cap healthcare business with a $291M market cap on $0 of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -92% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at -429% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $150M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, thin -194.7\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 11% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 2/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-6.4) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (16.4% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Healthcare peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (100% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.0},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom quartile among Healthcare peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Healthcare peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 102% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 13% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.7% return)"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Comparing Allogene Therapeutics (NASDAQ:ALLO) and Aktis Oncology (NASDAQ:AKTS)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/11/comparing-allogene-therapeutics-nasdaqallo-and-aktis-oncology-nasdaqakts.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794374118.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.909,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Allogene Therapeutics Reports First Clinical Data from Phase 1 RESOLUTION Study of ALLO-329 in Autoimmune Disease","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/healthcare/articles/allogene-therapeutics-reports-first-clinical-130000386.html","date":"2026-11-09","timestamp":1794229200.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.823,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Allogene Therapeutics (NASDAQ:ALLO) Stock Gets Downgrade from Wall Street Zen","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/09/allogene-therapeutics-nasdaqallo-stock-gets-downgrade-from-wall-street-zen.html","date":"2026-11-09","timestamp":1794207657.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.7,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["analyst_action"]},{"title":"Allogene targets ALPHA3 enrollment completio